
  <sn><md>### Local Path vs Remote Path in Rclone

The easiest way to understand Rclone is to separate **paths on your computer** from **paths on a configured storage service**.

| Concept                                  | Local Path                   | Remote Path                                |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Meaning                                  | Location on your computer    | Location inside a configured Rclone remote |
| Managed by                               | Operating system             | Rclone + storage provider                  |
| Example                                  | `/home/emon/Documents`       | `gdrive:Documents`                         |
| Requires Rclone configuration            | ❌ No                         | ✅ Yes                                      |
| Can be accessed normally by file manager | ✅ Yes                        | Depends on the provider/mount              |
| Storage location                         | SSD/HDD                      | Google Drive, S3, OneDrive, etc.           |
| Format                                   | OS filesystem path           | `remote-name:path`                         |
| Example file                             | `/home/emon/Documents/a.pdf` | `gdrive:Documents/a.pdf`                   |

</md></sn>
